     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>Theorem
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?> 
     <Lbl xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
       >
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>3.1
     </Lbl>
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?> 
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>(The additive structure of homology manifold bordism, Johnston [
     <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
       >
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>5
      <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
     </Link>
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>])
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>. 
    </Caption>
    <semantic-para xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
       rolemaps-to="Part"
      >
     <text-block xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
        xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
        Layout:TextAlign="Justify"
        rolemaps-to="P"
       >
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>…
     </text-block>
    </semantic-para>
   </theorem-like>
   <semantic-para xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
      rolemaps-to="Part"
     >
    <text-block xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
       xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
       Layout:TextAlign="Justify"
       rolemaps-to="P"
      >
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>For 
     <Formula xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
        title="math"
        af="mathml-8.xml source.tex"
        xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
        Layout:Placement="Inline"
       >
       <AssociatedFile name="mathml-8.xml" relationship="Supplement" media-type="application/mathml+xml" xmlns="">
       <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"> <mi>𝑚</mi> <mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">≥</mo> <mn>5</mn> </math>
       </AssociatedFile>
       <AssociatedFile name="source.tex" relationship="Supplement" media-type="application/x-tex" xmlns="">
       $m\geq 5$
       </AssociatedFile>
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>𝑚≥5
     </Formula>
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?> the Novikov-Wall surgery theory for topological manifolds gives an exact sequence (Wall [
     <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
       >
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>13
      <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
     </Link>
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>, Chapter 10].
    </text-block>
   </semantic-para>
   <semantic-para xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
      rolemaps-to="Part"
     >
    <text-block xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
       xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
       Layout:TextAlign="Justify"
       rolemaps-to="P"
      >
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>The surgery theory of topological manifolds was extended to homology man
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>ifolds in Quinn [
     <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
       >
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>9
      <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
     </Link>
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>, 
     <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
       >
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>10
      <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
     </Link>
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>] and Bryant, Ferry, Mio and Weinberger [
     <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
       >
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>1
      <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
     </Link>
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>].
    </text-block>
   </semantic-para>
   <semantic-para xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
      rolemaps-to="Part"
     >
    <text-block xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
       xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
       Layout:TextAlign="Justify"
       rolemaps-to="P"
      >
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>The 4-periodic obstruction is equivalent to an 
     <Formula xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
        title="math"
        af="mathml-9.xml source.tex"
        xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
        Layout:Placement="Inline"
       >
       <AssociatedFile name="mathml-9.xml" relationship="Supplement" media-type="application/mathml+xml" xmlns="">
       <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"> <mi>𝑚</mi> </math>
       </AssociatedFile>
       <AssociatedFile name="source.tex" relationship="Supplement" media-type="application/x-tex" xmlns="">
       $m$
       </AssociatedFile>
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>𝑚
     </Formula>
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>-dimensional homology man
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>ifold, by [
     <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
       >
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>1
      <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
     </Link>
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>].
    </text-block>
   </semantic-para>
   <semantic-para xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
      rolemaps-to="Part"
     >
    <text-block xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
       xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
       Layout:TextAlign="Justify"
       rolemaps-to="P"
      >
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>Thus, the surgery exact sequence of [
     <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
       >
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>1
      <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
     </Link>
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>] does not follow Wall [
     <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
       >
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>13
      <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
     </Link>
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>] in relating homology manifold structures and normal invariants.
    </text-block>
   </semantic-para>
   <semantic-para xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
      rolemaps-to="Part"
     >
    <text-block xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
       xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
       Layout:TextAlign="Justify"
       rolemaps-to="P"
      >
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>… the canonical 
     <Formula xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
        title="math"
        af="mathml-10.xml source.tex"
        xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
        Layout:Placement="Inline"
       >
       <AssociatedFile name="mathml-10.xml" relationship="Supplement" media-type="application/mathml+xml" xmlns="">
       <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"> <mi>𝑇</mi> <mi>𝑂</mi> <mi>𝑃</mi> </math>
       </AssociatedFile>
       <AssociatedFile name="source.tex" relationship="Supplement" media-type="application/x-tex" xmlns="">
       $TOP$
       </AssociatedFile>
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>𝑇𝑂𝑃
     </Formula>
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?> reduction ([
     <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
       >
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>3
      <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
     </Link>
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>]) of the Spivak normal fibration of 
     <Formula xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
        title="math"
        af="mathml-11.xml source.tex"
        xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
        Layout:Placement="Inline"
       >
       <AssociatedFile name="mathml-11.xml" relationship="Supplement" media-type="application/mathml+xml" xmlns="">
       <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"> <mi>𝑀</mi> </math>
       </AssociatedFile>
       <AssociatedFile name="source.tex" relationship="Supplement" media-type="application/x-tex" xmlns="">
       $M$
       </AssociatedFile>
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>𝑀
     </Formula>
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?> …
    </text-block>
   </semantic-para>
   <theorem-like xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
      rolemaps-to="Sect"
     >
    <Caption xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
      >
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>Theorem
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?> 
     <Lbl xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
       >
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>3.2
     </Lbl>
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?> 
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>(Johnston [
     <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
       >
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>5
      <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
     </Link>
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>])
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>. 
    </Caption>
    <semantic-para xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
       rolemaps-to="Part"
      >
     <text-block xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
        xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
        Layout:TextAlign="Justify"
        rolemaps-to="P"
       >
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>…
     </text-block>
    </semantic-para>
   </theorem-like>
   <semantic-para xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
      rolemaps-to="Part"
     >
    <text-block xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
       xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
       Layout:TextAlign="Justify"
       rolemaps-to="P"
      >
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>Actually [
     <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
       >
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>5
      <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
     </Link>
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>, (5.2)] is for 
     <Formula xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
        title="math"
        af="mathml-12.xml source.tex"
        xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
        Layout:Placement="Inline"
       >
       <AssociatedFile name="mathml-12.xml" relationship="Supplement" media-type="application/mathml+xml" xmlns="">
       <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"> <mi>𝑚</mi> <mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">≥</mo> <mn>7</mn> </math>
       </AssociatedFile>
       <AssociatedFile name="source.tex" relationship="Supplement" media-type="application/x-tex" xmlns="">
       $m\geq 7$
       </AssociatedFile>
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>𝑚≥7
     </Formula>
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>, but we can improve to 
     <Formula xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
        title="math"
        af="mathml-13.xml source.tex"
        xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
        Layout:Placement="Inline"
       >
       <AssociatedFile name="mathml-13.xml" relationship="Supplement" media-type="application/mathml+xml" xmlns="">
       <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"> <mi>𝑚</mi> <mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">≥</mo> <mn>6</mn> </math>
       </AssociatedFile>
       <AssociatedFile name="source.tex" relationship="Supplement" media-type="application/x-tex" xmlns="">
       $m\geq 6$
       </AssociatedFile>
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>𝑚≥6
     </Formula>
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?> by a slight variation of the proof as described below.
